  "definition": "Lottery Commission Reporting",
  "effectiveDate": "2010-04-02",
  "historyNote": "#9689-B, eff 4-2-10 (a) The Lottery Commission shall withhold all tax due and payable to the state from any payout of gambling winnings. (b) All amounts withheld shall be delivered to the department or deposited with Treasury where applicable on a monthly basis by the 15th day of the month.",
  "inScheme": "https://granitestate.github.io/rules/scheme",
  "notation": "Rev 3103.03",
  "officialHtml": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/rev3100.html",
  "prefLabel": "Rev 3103.03 Lottery Commission Reporting",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Rev 3103.03 Lottery Commission Reporting.\n\n(a) The Lottery Commission shall provide taxpayer information to the department in an electronic format.\n\n(b) Such information shall include the taxpayer’s name, address, taxpayer identification number as defined in Rev 2902.02, the amount of gambling winnings paid during the calendar year, whether said winnings are paid in single or multiple installments, and the amount of tax withheld by the Lottery Commission.\n\n(c) This information shall be transmitted by the Lottery Commission to the department on a monthly basis by the 15th day of the month.\n\nSource. #9689-B, eff 4-2-10\n\n(a) The Lottery Commission shall withhold all tax due and payable to the state from any payout of gambling winnings.\n\n(b) All amounts withheld shall be delivered to the department or deposited with Treasury where applicable on a monthly basis by the 15th day of the month.\n\nSource. #9689-B, eff 4-2-10",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/rev3100.html"
